    "</div>\r\n<details><summary>原始讨论（英文，仅供参考）</summary><div class=\"source-discussion i18n-noloc\" lang=\"en\">tumi983 days, 18 hours ago<br>Selected Answer: B<br>Independent analysis tasks execute concurrently, reducing total batch processing time. Bedrock timeouts and CloudWatch provide<br>appropriate operational controls.<br>upvoted 1 times<br>blieskies2 weeks, 5 days ago<br>Selected Answer: B<br>I accept it&#x27;s B because this processing required parallelisation but I wish they&#x27;d suggested MAP instead of PARALLEL because it we assume<br>that each step for a report takes the same amount of time then it&#x27;d still take 45/3 seconds = 15 seconds .. whereas parallel would have given<br>us a tidy 45/5 = 9 seconds (under the SLA) requirement<br>upvoted 1 times<br>Chibuzo13 months ago<br>Selected Answer: B<br>The core problem is a 45-second sequential process that must finish in 10 seconds — a 4.5x speedup requirement. The only way to achieve<br>this without faster hardware is parallelization. Option B directly addresses this with Step Functions&#x27; Parallel state, which fans out multiple<br>Lambda invocations simultaneously across analysis types (financial data, sentiment, compliance). Since these three workloads are<br>independent of each other, running them concurrently collapses wall-clock time dramatically. CloudWatch integration for latency tracking is<br>a practical operational addition, not overhead.<br>upvoted 1 times<br>de1612d5 months, 1 week ago<br>Selected Answer: B<br>I want to parallelize batch processing, so the answer is B.<br>upvoted 1 times<br>a9fb7b25 months, 3 weeks ago<br>Selected Answer: B<br>Step Functions workflow can invoke separate Lambda functions in parallel for different analysis tasks, which is exactly what this batch<br>pattern needs. Can also monitor execution time and Bedrock/model latency with CloudWatch metrics, which helps verify the system stays<br>under the 10-second target. Amazon Bedrock exposes monitoring through CloudWatch, and CloudWatch generative AI observability<br>includes latency views for model invocations.<br>upvoted 2 times<br>eesa6 months, 1 week ago<br>Selected Answer: B<br>AWS Step Functions con Parallel state (Opción B) - MEJOR SOLUCIÓN:<br>✅ Paralelización efectiva: Procesa múltiples análisis (financiero, sentimiento, compliance) simultáneamente en lugar de secuencialmente<br>✅ Reduce tiempo drásticamente: De 45s a ~10s al ejecutar tareas en paralelo<br>✅ Orquestación robusta: Step Functions maneja la coordinación de múltiples Lambda functions<br>✅ Monitoreo integrado: CloudWatch metrics para tracking de latencia y tiempos<br>✅ Manejo de errores: Retry logic y error handling nativos<br>✅ Escalabilidad: Cada tipo de análisis escala independientemente<br>upvoted 2 times<br>Neos036 months, 1 week ago<br>Selected Answer: A<br>A is correct<br>upvoted 1 times<br>GiorgioGss6 months, 2 weeks ago<br>Selected Answer: B<br>ACD fail because it ads latency.<br>upvoted 2 times<br>67bdb196 months, 2 weeks ago<br>Selected Answer: C<br>Feels like C is the one. Does anyone disagree?<br>upvoted 1 times</div></details></details></div>"
