    "</div>\r\n<details><summary>原始讨论（英文，仅供参考）</summary><div class=\"source-discussion i18n-noloc\" lang=\"en\">Nowax1 week, 1 day ago<br>Selected Answer: A<br>SAML 2.0 is the standard Entra ID-&gt;IAM enterprise SSO pattern; department IAM roles scoped to model ARNs enforce family-level access;<br>&#x27;bedrock-runtime&#x27; PrivateLink endpoints keep inference off the internet; and CloudTrail (API activity) plus model invocation logging<br>(prompt/response bodies) together give the complete trail.<br>Not B - NAT gateway egress reaches the public Bedrock endpoint, so traffic leaves the private path, and CloudWatch Logs captures nothing<br>unless invocation logging is enabled.<br>Not C - &quot;public endpoints with VPC routing&quot; is not a private path, permissions boundaries cap rather than grant, and CloudTrail alone omits<br>prompt/response content.<br>And not D - Entra ID has no visibility into Bedrock invocations, so it cannot be the audit trail, and SCPs are account-wide guardrails, not per-<br>department grants.<br>upvoted 1 times</div></details></details></div>"
