    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 156–158 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">RIVERSIDE — Millbrook Cycles, the family-owned bicycle shop that has operated on Canal Street for more than thirty years, announced this week that it will open a second location in the Eastgate neighborhood this fall.\r\n\r\nOwner Dana Millbrook said the expansion was driven by growing demand for repairs and commuter bicycles. &quot;We&#x27;ve seen more people cycling to work, especially since the city added protected bike lanes downtown,&quot; she said. &quot;Our current shop simply can&#x27;t keep up with the repair volume.&quot;\r\n\r\nThe new store will focus on servicing and rentals rather than sales, and it will employ six technicians, four of whom will be hired locally. Ms. Millbrook noted that the Canal Street location will remain the company&#x27;s main showroom.\r\n\r\nA grand-opening event, featuring free safety checks and a group ride along the river trail, is planned for October.</div>\r\n",
