    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 162–164 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.harlowmuseum.org/visit\r\n\r\nPlan Your Visit — Harlow Museum of Design\r\n\r\nHours: Tuesday–Sunday, 10 A.M.–6 P.M. Closed Mondays and public holidays.\r\n\r\nAdmission: General admission is $18; students and seniors pay $12. Children under 12 and museum members enter free. On the first Thursday evening of each month, from 5 to 9 P.M., admission is free for everyone thanks to the support of the Callan Foundation.\r\n\r\nGetting Here: The museum is a short walk from Central Station. Paid parking is available in the lot on Vernon Street, but spaces are limited, so we encourage visitors to use public transit.\r\n\r\nAccessibility: All galleries are wheelchair accessible, and wheelchairs may be borrowed free of charge at the information desk. Please note that large bags must be checked in the cloakroom before entering the galleries.</div>\r\n",
