    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 172–175 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Ferndale Foods to Power Plant with Solar Energy\r\n\r\nFERNDALE (May 8) — Ferndale Foods, one of the region&#x27;s largest food-processing companies, announced yesterday that it will install solar panels across the roof of its main production facility. — [1] —. The project, expected to be completed by the end of the year, will supply roughly 40 percent of the plant&#x27;s electricity.\r\n\r\nCompany president Alan Reyes said the investment reflects both environmental and financial goals. — [2] —. &quot;Generating our own power protects us from rising prices and helps us meet our sustainability targets,&quot; he explained.\r\n\r\nThe installation will be carried out by SunRidge Solar, a local firm that has completed similar projects for several area businesses. — [3] —. Ferndale Foods estimates that the panels will pay for themselves within seven years through lower energy bills.\r\n\r\nThe announcement was welcomed by city officials, who have encouraged local employers to adopt cleaner technologies. — [4] —. A ribbon-cutting ceremony is planned once the system is switched on.</div>\r\n",
