    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 156–158 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">OAKDALE — Sunrise Bakery, a neighborhood fixture on Chestnut Street for over twenty years, will begin offering cooking and baking classes next month, owner Marco Ferreira announced this week.\r\n\r\nThe classes grew out of frequent customer requests. &quot;People kept asking how we make our sourdough,&quot; Mr. Ferreira said. &quot;Eventually I realized there was real interest in learning, not just buying.&quot;\r\n\r\nHeld in the bakery&#x27;s expanded back kitchen, the evening classes will cover breads, pastries, and cakes, with no more than eight students per session so that everyone gets hands-on time. Mr. Ferreira said the bakery&#x27;s regular retail hours will not change.\r\n\r\nThe first session, on bread basics, is already fully booked, and a waiting list has opened for future dates.</div>\r\n",
