    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 162–164 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.pinehillpark.org/plan\r\n\r\nPlan Your Visit — Pine Hill Nature Park\r\n\r\nHours: Open daily from dawn to dusk, year-round. The visitor center is open 9 A.M.–4 P.M.\r\n\r\nAdmission: Entry to the park is free. A small fee of $5 per vehicle applies at the main parking area; walkers and cyclists enter at no charge. Guided nature walks, offered every Saturday at 10 A.M., are free but require advance booking, as group sizes are capped.\r\n\r\nTrails: The park has twelve miles of marked trails, ranging from easy to challenging. Trail maps are available at the visitor center or can be downloaded from this site.\r\n\r\nPlease help us protect the park: keep dogs on a leash, carry out all litter, and do not pick the wildflowers.</div>\r\n",
