    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 165–167 refer to the following Review.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Reviewed by Amara D.  ★★★★☆\r\nDinner at Solstice Bistro\r\n\r\nSolstice Bistro was a pleasant surprise for a Tuesday night out. The dining room is small but warmly lit, and our table by the window had a lovely view of the harbor. The seasonal menu changes weekly, and our server was genuinely knowledgeable, recommending a grilled-fish special that turned out to be the highlight of the meal.\r\n\r\nService was attentive without being intrusive. My only quibble is that the restaurant does not take reservations, so we waited about twenty-five minutes for a table, even on a quiet evening. Arriving early would be my advice.\r\n\r\nThe prices are fair for the quality, and I&#x27;ll certainly be back — next time, a little earlier.</div>\r\n",
