    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 168–171 refer to the following Letter.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Brightwater Utilities\r\n100 Cedar Lane, Kelston\r\n\r\nNovember 8\r\n\r\nDear Mr. Feldman,\r\n\r\nWe are writing to let you know about scheduled maintenance that will temporarily affect water service to your neighborhood. On Tuesday, November 18, between 9:00 A.M. and 2:00 P.M., crews will replace an aging section of the main pipe on Cedar Lane.\r\n\r\nDuring these hours, your water supply will be shut off. We recommend storing enough water for drinking and basic needs beforehand. When service resumes, you may notice that the water appears slightly cloudy for a short time; this is harmless and will clear if you run the cold tap for a few minutes.\r\n\r\nNo action is required on your part, and there will be no charge for this work. We have chosen a midweek daytime window to minimize disruption to households.\r\n\r\nWe appreciate your patience as we work to keep your water system reliable.\r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\nBrightwater Utilities</div>\r\n",
