    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 172–175 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Cyprus Textiles Adds Night Shift to Meet Demand\r\n\r\nBRADLEY (March 3) — Cyprus Textiles, a manufacturer of upholstery fabric, announced it will add a full night shift at its Bradley plant beginning next month. — [1] —. The move is expected to create about 60 new jobs in the area.\r\n\r\nManaging director Nadia Petrou said orders had risen sharply over the past year, particularly from furniture makers. — [2] —. &quot;We simply cannot keep up with demand on a single daytime shift,&quot; she said.\r\n\r\nThe company plans to recruit and train new workers over the coming weeks, with priority given to local applicants. — [3] —. Existing employees will not be required to change their hours.\r\n\r\nCommunity leaders welcomed the announcement. — [4] —. A local college has offered to run a short training course for those hoping to apply.</div>\r\n",
