    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 181–185 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.riverkeepers.org/join\r\n\r\nRiverkeepers — Volunteer Program Coordinator (Part-Time)\r\n\r\nRiverkeepers is a nonprofit dedicated to protecting the Marrow River watershed. We are seeking a part-time Volunteer Program Coordinator to organize our growing community of volunteers.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n• Recruit, schedule, and support volunteers for cleanup and monitoring events\r\n• Maintain the volunteer database and send weekly updates\r\n• Represent Riverkeepers at community fairs\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n• At least two years of experience coordinating volunteers or events\r\n• Excellent organizational and communication skills\r\n• Comfortable working some weekends, as many events are held on Saturdays\r\n• Experience with database software is an asset but not essential\r\n\r\nThis is a 20-hour-per-week position with a flexible weekday schedule. To apply, email your résumé and a brief statement of interest to jobs@riverkeepers.org by April 30.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: jobs@riverkeepers.org\r\nFrom: h.nakamura@mail.com\r\nSubject: Application — Volunteer Program Coordinator\r\nDate: April 18\r\n\r\nDear Hiring Committee,\r\n\r\nI am writing to apply for the Volunteer Program Coordinator position. My résumé and statement of interest are attached.\r\n\r\nFor the past three years, I have coordinated volunteers for a city food bank, where I scheduled more than fifty people each month and ran two large fundraising fairs. I am highly organized and enjoy keeping teams motivated and informed. I am also confident with database tools, having managed our food bank&#x27;s donor system.\r\n\r\nI understand that many of your events fall on weekends, and I want to note that I am fully available on Saturdays. I am excited about the chance to support the Marrow River watershed and would welcome the opportunity to discuss my application.\r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\nHana Nakamura</div>\r\n",
