    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 191–195 refer to the following Advertisement.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">WESTON ADULT EDUCATION CENTER\r\nWinter Evening Courses\r\n\r\nLearn something new this winter! Our evening courses are taught by experienced instructors and meet once a week for six weeks. Class sizes are small, so early registration is encouraged.\r\n\r\nThis term&#x27;s courses:\r\n• Beginning Watercolor Painting\r\n• Home Bookkeeping\r\n• Intermediate French\r\n• Creative Writing\r\n\r\nFees: $90 per course, or $160 for any two. All materials are included except for Watercolor Painting, for which students must bring their own brushes. Center members receive a 20 percent discount.\r\n\r\nRegister online at www.westonadulted.org or by phone by January 5.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Winter Evening Course Schedule — Weston Adult Education Center\r\nAll classes run 6:00–7:30 P.M.\r\n\r\nCourse ............................ Day ......... Room\r\nBeginning Watercolor Painting .... Monday ...... Studio 1\r\nHome Bookkeeping ................. Tuesday ..... Room 4\r\nIntermediate French .............. Wednesday ... Room 2\r\nCreative Writing ................. Thursday .... Room 2\r\n\r\nClasses begin the week of January 12. Please arrive a few minutes early to the first class to collect any handouts.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: info@westonadulted.org\r\nFrom: d.moreau@mail.com\r\nSubject: Question about my registration\r\nDate: January 3\r\n\r\nHello,\r\n\r\nI signed up last week for two courses — Home Bookkeeping and Creative Writing — and I&#x27;m looking forward to starting. I just want to double-check the schedule.\r\n\r\nCould you confirm that the two courses meet on different evenings? I have a standing commitment on Tuesday nights, so if there is a conflict I may need to switch. If Home Bookkeeping is on a night I can&#x27;t attend, could I move into Intermediate French instead?\r\n\r\nAlso, I am a center member, so I believe the member discount should apply to my total.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\nDenise Moreau</div>\r\n",
