    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 196–200 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Chapters &amp; Co. Opens Flagship Store With Café\r\n\r\nChapters &amp; Co., the independent bookseller, opened its largest store yet on Halden Square last weekend. The new location is the first to include a full café and the first to stay open until 9 P.M. on weeknights.\r\n\r\nTo mark the opening, the store is offering a free coffee with any book purchase through the end of the month. It has also launched a mobile app that lets customers reserve books online and earn a store credit for every ten purchases.\r\n\r\n&quot;Our customers told us they wanted a place to linger, not just shop,&quot; said owner Beatrice Lund. Reader feedback, she added, shapes the store&#x27;s events calendar, which now includes weekly author readings.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">★★★☆☆  Reviewed by Sanjay P.\r\n\r\nI stopped by the new Chapters &amp; Co. on a Thursday evening, mainly because I&#x27;d heard it stays open late — perfect after work. The café was cozy, the staff were welcoming, and I loved the free-coffee promotion.\r\n\r\nMy one frustration was the app. I tried to reserve a book online, but it kept freezing at the checkout screen and never recorded my purchase for store credit. I ended up reserving at the counter instead. The staff were apologetic and sorted it out quickly. I&#x27;ll be back for the atmosphere and the late hours, but I hope the app gets fixed.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: sanjay.p@mail.com\r\nFrom: b.lund@chaptersandco.com\r\nSubject: Thank you for your feedback\r\nDate: October 5\r\n\r\nDear Sanjay,\r\n\r\nThank you for visiting our new Halden Square store and for taking the time to review it. I&#x27;m so glad you enjoyed the café and our extended weeknight hours, but I&#x27;m sorry the app gave you trouble.\r\n\r\nOur technical team has since fixed the checkout problem you described, and the store-credit feature is now working correctly. As an apology, I&#x27;ve added a $15 store credit to your account, which you&#x27;ll see the next time you log in.\r\n\r\nFeedback like yours is invaluable, and it helps us improve. I hope to welcome you back soon.\r\n\r\nWarm regards,\r\nBeatrice Lund\r\nOwner, Chapters &amp; Co.</div>\r\n",
