    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 172–175 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Northgate Mall to Add Rooftop Solar Panels\r\n\r\nNORTHGATE (July 2) — Northgate Mall announced that it will install solar panels across its entire rooftop beginning this autumn. — [1] —. The panels are expected to supply about a third of the mall&#x27;s electricity once fully operational.\r\n\r\nCenter manager Dana Cole said the decision was driven by both cost and environmental concerns. — [2] —. &quot;Energy is one of our biggest expenses, and this puts some of that back in our control,&quot; she said.\r\n\r\nThe work will be carried out by SolAura Energy, a regional firm that has fitted panels on several shopping centers. — [3] —. The mall estimates the system will pay for itself in about eight years.\r\n\r\nShoppers will see little disruption, as most of the work will take place overnight. — [4] —. A viewing area explaining how the system works is planned for the main concourse.</div>\r\n",
