    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 181–185 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.brightorchard.com/careers\r\n\r\nBright Orchard — Marketing Assistant (Downtown Office)\r\n\r\nBright Orchard is a growing organic-juice brand looking for a Marketing Assistant to support our small, energetic team.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n• Schedule and post content across our social media channels\r\n• Help plan in-store tasting events\r\n• Track campaign results and prepare simple monthly reports\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n• At least one year of experience in marketing or communications\r\n• Strong writing skills and attention to detail\r\n• Comfortable using spreadsheets to organize data\r\n• Experience with graphic-design software such as Canva is a plus but not required\r\n\r\nWe offer a friendly workplace, health coverage, and a monthly product allowance. This is a full-time, in-office role.\r\n\r\nTo apply, send your résumé and a short cover letter to careers@brightorchard.com by May 10.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: careers@brightorchard.com\r\nFrom: lena.fischer@mail.com\r\nSubject: Application for Marketing Assistant\r\nDate: April 29\r\n\r\nDear Hiring Team,\r\n\r\nI&#x27;m excited to apply for the Marketing Assistant role. My résumé and cover letter are attached.\r\n\r\nSince graduating two years ago, I have worked as a communications assistant at a local nonprofit, where I managed our social media calendar and wrote our monthly email newsletter. I&#x27;m very comfortable with spreadsheets, having tracked all of our campaign results in one. Although it wasn&#x27;t part of my job, I taught myself Canva and now design most of our simple graphics.\r\n\r\nI love the idea of working for a food-and-drink brand and would be thrilled to help plan your tasting events. Thank you for your consideration.\r\n\r\nBest,\r\nLena Fischer</div>\r\n",
