    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 156–158 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">HAVERTON — Copperline Roasters, a coffee company that has supplied cafés across the county for a decade, will open a public training lab on Ferndale Street this summer, founder Camille Ndiaye announced.\r\n\r\nThe lab grew out of interest from the roaster&#x27;s wholesale clients. &quot;Café owners kept asking us to teach their staff how to brew consistently,&quot; Ms. Ndiaye said. &quot;Rather than travel to each shop, we decided to build one space where anyone can learn.&quot;\r\n\r\nThe lab will host small hands-on sessions on brewing, tasting, and equipment care, capped at twelve participants so each person gets time at the bar. Ms. Ndiaye emphasized that the company&#x27;s wholesale roasting operation will not be affected and will continue at its current facility.\r\n\r\nThe first block of classes sold out within days, and a second block has already been scheduled for the fall.</div>\r\n",
