    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 162–164 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.marlanaquarium.org/visit\r\n\r\nPlan Your Visit — Marlan Bay Aquarium\r\n\r\nHours: Open daily, 9:30 A.M.–5:30 P.M. Last entry is at 4:30 P.M.\r\n\r\nAdmission: Adults $22, children ages 3–12 $14, under 3 free. Members enter free all year. Tickets bought online are $2 cheaper than at the gate, and we recommend booking ahead on weekends, when timed entry slots often sell out.\r\n\r\nGetting Here: The aquarium sits on the harbor, a five-minute walk from the Bay Street tram stop. Parking is scarce nearby, so we suggest arriving by tram or bus.\r\n\r\nDaily Programs: Free feeding talks take place at the main tank at 11 A.M. and 3 P.M., and touch-pool sessions run hourly. All programs are included with admission and require no separate booking.</div>\r\n",
