    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 165–167 refer to the following Review.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Reviewed by Dominic R.  ★★★★☆\r\nAeris X2 Noise-Canceling Headphones\r\n\r\nI bought the Aeris X2 mainly for long train commutes, and they have transformed my daily ride. The noise cancellation is genuinely impressive; the rumble of the carriage all but disappears once I switch it on. The padding is soft, and I can wear them for two hours without discomfort.\r\n\r\nBattery life is the standout feature — I charge them once a week at most. My only real complaint is the carrying case, which is bulky and doesn&#x27;t fit easily into a laptop bag. I also wish the controls were a bit easier to find by touch.\r\n\r\nStill, for the price, these are excellent, and I&#x27;d recommend them to anyone who commutes.</div>\r\n",
