    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 172–175 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Brookvale Offices to Install Electric-Vehicle Chargers\r\n\r\nBROOKVALE (May 6) — Brookvale Business Park, home to more than forty companies, announced that it will install electric-vehicle charging stations throughout its parking areas beginning this autumn. — [1] —. The first phase will add twenty chargers, with room to expand as demand grows.\r\n\r\nPark director Louisa Prendergast said the project responds to requests from tenant firms. — [2] —. &quot;Several of our companies have shifted to electric fleets, and their staff have been asking where to plug in,&quot; she said.\r\n\r\nThe installation will be handled by VoltEdge Systems, a firm that has equipped a number of office campuses in the region. — [3] —. Charging will be free for the first six months, after which a modest per-session fee will apply.\r\n\r\nTenants have welcomed the plan. — [4] —. A short guide explaining how to use the chargers will be circulated before they go live.</div>\r\n",
