    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 191–195 refer to the following Advertisement.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">RIVERSTONE COOKING SCHOOL\r\nSummer Weeknight Classes\r\n\r\nCook something new this summer! Our hands-on evening classes are taught by professional chefs and meet once a week for four weeks. Kitchens are small, so seats fill quickly — book early.\r\n\r\nThis term&#x27;s classes:\r\n• Fresh Pasta from Scratch\r\n• Everyday Thai Cooking\r\n• Bread and Focaccia\r\n• Knife Skills Basics\r\n\r\nFees: $110 per class, or $200 for any two. All ingredients are provided; just bring an apron. Cooking club members receive a 20 percent discount.\r\n\r\nRegister online at www.riverstonecook.com or at the front desk by June 15.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Summer Weeknight Class Schedule — Riverstone Cooking School\r\nAll sessions run 6:00–8:00 P.M.\r\n\r\nClass ............................ Day ......... Kitchen\r\nFresh Pasta from Scratch ......... Monday ...... Kitchen 1\r\nEveryday Thai Cooking ............ Tuesday ..... Kitchen 2\r\nBread and Focaccia ............... Tuesday ..... Kitchen 3\r\nKnife Skills Basics .............. Thursday .... Kitchen 1\r\n\r\nClasses begin the week of June 22. Please arrive ten minutes early to your first session to collect your apron loaner if needed.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: info@riverstonecook.com\r\nFrom: marcus.hale@mail.com\r\nSubject: Question about my class dates\r\nDate: June 10\r\n\r\nHello,\r\n\r\nI registered last week for two classes — Everyday Thai Cooking and Bread and Focaccia — and I&#x27;m looking forward to them. But I want to make sure I haven&#x27;t double-booked myself.\r\n\r\nCould you confirm whether the two classes meet on the same evening? I can only attend one class per night, so if they clash I&#x27;d like to move Bread and Focaccia to Knife Skills Basics instead.\r\n\r\nAlso, I&#x27;m a cooking club member, so I believe the member discount should apply to my total.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\nMarcus Hale</div>\r\n",
