    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 156–158 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">WESTON — Tidewater Pottery, a studio that has sold handmade ceramics at the Weston craft market for twelve years, will open a permanent storefront on Alder Street next month, owner Priscilla Vaughan announced.\r\n\r\nThe move follows steady growth in demand. &quot;At the market we could only sell what fit on a single table,&quot; Ms. Vaughan said. &quot;Customers kept asking where they could see the full range, so a proper shop made sense.&quot;\r\n\r\nThe new store will display the studio&#x27;s complete collection and will also host occasional weekend demonstrations, where visitors can watch pieces being thrown on the wheel. Ms. Vaughan noted that the studio will keep its market stall as well, to reach weekend shoppers.\r\n\r\nA soft opening is planned for the first Saturday of next month, with a larger celebration to follow later in the season.</div>\r\n",
