      "slot": "question.60"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 162–164 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.thornfieldgardens.com/tickets\r\n\r\nVisitor Information — Thornfield Historic Gardens\r\n\r\nHours: Open Wednesday–Sunday, 10 A.M.–5 P.M. Closed Mondays and Tuesdays.\r\n\r\nAdmission: Adults $16, seniors and students $11, children under 10 free. A family ticket (two adults and up to three children) is $40. Season passes offer unlimited visits and are excellent value for frequent guests.\r\n\r\nGetting Here: Thornfield is a fifteen-minute bus ride from the town center; the number 9 bus stops directly outside the gates. On-site parking is plentiful and free for all visitors.\r\n\r\nGuided Tours: Volunteer-led tours of the walled garden depart at 11 A.M. and 2 P.M. and last about forty-five minutes. Tours are included with admission but have limited spaces, so please sign up at the ticket booth on arrival.</div>\r\n",
