    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 172–175 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Larkspur Dairy to Open On-Site Visitor Center\r\n\r\nLARKSPUR (April 4) — Larkspur Dairy, one of the region&#x27;s oldest family farms, announced it will open a visitor center at its property this summer. — [1] —. The center will feature a viewing gallery over the bottling line, a small museum of farming tools, and a shop selling the farm&#x27;s cheeses.\r\n\r\nOwner Gareth Pell said the project reflects growing public curiosity about where food comes from. — [2] —. &quot;People want to see how milk gets from the field to the carton, and we&#x27;re happy to show them,&quot; he said.\r\n\r\nThe center will be built in a renovated barn near the main entrance and staffed by both farm workers and seasonal guides. — [3] —. Admission will be free, though the farm hopes visitors will stop by the shop on their way out.\r\n\r\nLocal tourism officials praised the plan. — [4] —. A ribbon-cutting is planned for the opening weekend, with tastings of the farm&#x27;s newest cheese.</div>\r\n",
