    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 181–185 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.brightpathpublishing.com/careers\r\n\r\nBrightpath Publishing — Editorial Assistant (Kingsport Office)\r\n\r\nBrightpath Publishing produces travel and cookery titles. We are seeking an Editorial Assistant to support our editors through every stage of the publishing process.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n• Proofread manuscripts and check facts\r\n• Coordinate schedules between authors and designers\r\n• Maintain the editorial calendar and meeting notes\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n• A bachelor&#x27;s degree in English, journalism, or a related field\r\n• At least one year of experience in an office or publishing setting\r\n• Excellent attention to detail\r\n• Familiarity with a project-management tool such as Trello is preferred but not required\r\n\r\nWe offer a collaborative team, health benefits, and a yearly book allowance. This is a full-time, on-site role.\r\n\r\nTo apply, send your résumé and a short cover letter to careers@brightpathpublishing.com by August 5. Applications are reviewed as they arrive.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: careers@brightpathpublishing.com\r\nFrom: elias.norberg@mail.com\r\nSubject: Application for Editorial Assistant\r\nDate: July 21\r\n\r\nDear Hiring Team,\r\n\r\nI am writing to apply for the Editorial Assistant position. My résumé and cover letter are attached.\r\n\r\nI graduated two years ago with a degree in journalism, and for the past eighteen months I have worked as an office assistant at a small magazine, where I proofread articles and kept our production schedule on track. I have a sharp eye for detail and enjoy the careful work of catching errors before they reach print. Although the posting lists it as optional, I have used the Trello project-management tool to organize our magazine&#x27;s workflow and find it invaluable.\r\n\r\nI would be thrilled to contribute to Brightpath&#x27;s travel and cookery list. Thank you for considering my application.\r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\nElias Norberg</div>\r\n",
