    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 196–200 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">CityWheels Car Sharing Expands to Maple Ridge\r\n\r\nCityWheels, the hourly car-sharing service, added the Maple Ridge neighborhood to its network this week, its first location with vehicles parked directly on residential streets rather than in central lots. Members can now find a car within a short walk of most homes in the area.\r\n\r\nTo celebrate, CityWheels is waiving the annual membership fee for anyone who joins before the end of the month. The company also released an updated app that shows real-time vehicle locations and awards a free hour of driving for every ten trips completed.\r\n\r\n&quot;Our members told us the biggest hurdle was walking twenty minutes to reach a car,&quot; said operations lead Farid Naderi. &quot;Putting vehicles on neighborhood streets solves that.&quot;</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">★★★☆☆  Reviewed by Priya D.\r\n\r\nI joined CityWheels as soon as it came to Maple Ridge, mainly because there&#x27;s now a car parked just around the corner from me — no more long walks to the lot. The car was clean, fuel was full, and booking was quick.\r\n\r\nMy complaint is the app. It showed the nearest vehicle correctly, but when I tried to extend my booking it kept crashing, and my free-hour credit never appeared after my tenth trip. I had to call support to extend the time. They were friendly and sorted it out. I&#x27;ll stay for the convenience, but the app has bugs.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: priya.d@mail.com\r\nFrom: f.naderi@citywheels.com\r\nSubject: Thank you for your feedback\r\nDate: May 22\r\n\r\nDear Priya,\r\n\r\nThank you for joining CityWheels in Maple Ridge and for taking the time to review us. I&#x27;m glad the nearby parking made things easier, but I&#x27;m sorry the app gave you trouble.\r\n\r\nOur engineering team has fixed the crash you experienced when extending a booking, and the free-hour credit is now applied correctly. As an apology, I&#x27;ve added three free driving hours to your account, which you&#x27;ll see the next time you open the app.\r\n\r\nFeedback like yours is genuinely valuable and helps us make the service better. I hope your next trip is trouble-free.\r\n\r\nWarm regards,\r\nFarid Naderi\r\nOperations Lead, CityWheels</div>\r\n",
