    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 156–158 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">FAIRHAVEN — Meadow Lane Florist, a shop that has arranged flowers for Fairhaven weddings for fifteen years, will begin offering flower-arranging workshops next month, owner Rosalind Pike announced this week.\r\n\r\nThe classes are a response to frequent customer interest. &quot;Brides and guests kept asking if we taught arranging, not just made the bouquets,&quot; Ms. Pike said. &quot;There&#x27;s clearly an appetite for learning the craft.&quot;\r\n\r\nThe evening workshops will be held in the shop&#x27;s newly cleared back room, with no more than ten participants per session so that each person receives individual guidance. Ms. Pike stressed that the shop&#x27;s wedding and event business will carry on without change.\r\n\r\nThe first two sessions filled up within a week, and the shop is now keeping a waiting list for later dates.</div>\r\n",
