    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 159–161 refer to the following Memo.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">MEMORANDUM\r\n\r\nTo: All Laboratory Staff\r\nFrom: Dr. Anwar Haddad, Lab Director\r\nDate: January 12\r\nRe: New sample-logging system\r\n\r\nBeginning Monday, January 26, all incoming samples must be logged in our new digital tracking system, LabTrace, instead of the paper intake sheets. This will reduce lost samples and let anyone check a sample&#x27;s status instantly.\r\n\r\nWhen a sample arrives, scan its barcode into LabTrace, select the assigned test, and note the requesting department. The system will generate a tracking number, which should be written on the sample container. Please store samples in the labeled refrigerators as usual.\r\n\r\nPlease note that the paper intake sheets will be removed from the receiving bench, so do not continue using them. Training sessions will be held on January 20 and 21; sign up on the board by the door.</div>\r\n",
