    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 162–164 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.summitpeakpark.org/plan\r\n\r\nPlan Your Visit — Summit Peak Adventure Park\r\n\r\nHours: Open daily, 9 A.M.–6 P.M. from April to October. The park is closed during the winter months.\r\n\r\nAdmission: A day pass is $28 for adults and $18 for children under 14. Season passes offer unlimited visits and are our best value for families. Groups of ten or more receive a 15 percent discount when booked in advance.\r\n\r\nGetting Here: The park is a twenty-minute drive from the town center. A free shuttle runs from the train station every half hour on weekends. Parking on-site is ample.\r\n\r\nSafety: All climbing activities require closed-toe shoes and a signed waiver, which can be completed online before your visit to save time at the gate. Children under 14 must be accompanied by an adult on the high courses.</div>\r\n",
