    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 172–175 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Hartwell Library to Add Community Makerspace\r\n\r\nHARTWELL (June 9) — The Hartwell Public Library announced it will open a community makerspace on its lower floor this autumn. — [1] —. The space will offer 3D printers, sewing machines, and hand tools that any library member can use free of charge.\r\n\r\nLibrary director Naomi Osei said the idea grew from patron surveys. — [2] —. &quot;People told us they wanted a place to build and repair things, not just borrow books,&quot; she said.\r\n\r\nThe makerspace will be set up in a storeroom that has sat unused for years. — [3] —. Volunteers with technical backgrounds will be on hand during opening hours to help newcomers get started.\r\n\r\nCity council members welcomed the project. — [4] —. A weekend of free demonstrations is planned to introduce the equipment to the public.</div>\r\n",
