    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 181–185 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.terraformlandscapes.com/careers\r\n\r\nTerraform Landscapes — Garden Design Assistant (Millbrook Studio)\r\n\r\nTerraform Landscapes designs gardens for homes and small commercial sites. We are hiring a Garden Design Assistant to support our designers from concept to planting.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n• Prepare planting plans and material lists under a designer&#x27;s direction\r\n• Visit sites to take measurements and photographs\r\n• Liaise with nurseries and contractors on availability\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n• A diploma or degree in horticulture, landscape design, or a related field\r\n• At least one year of experience in a garden or design setting\r\n• A valid driver&#x27;s license, as sites are spread across the region\r\n• Skill with garden-design software such as SketchUp is an asset but not required\r\n\r\nWe offer a friendly studio, health benefits, and paid time to attend industry shows. This is a full-time role.\r\n\r\nTo apply, send your résumé and a short portfolio to careers@terraformlandscapes.com by July 15.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: careers@terraformlandscapes.com\r\nFrom: amara.dlamini@mail.com\r\nSubject: Application — Garden Design Assistant\r\nDate: July 2\r\n\r\nDear Hiring Team,\r\n\r\nI would like to apply for the Garden Design Assistant position. My résumé and a short portfolio are attached.\r\n\r\nI completed a diploma in horticulture two years ago, and for the past two years I have worked at a garden center, where I advised customers on planting plans and helped design several small display gardens. I hold a full driver&#x27;s license and am happy to travel to sites. Although the posting lists it as optional, I taught myself SketchUp and use it to sketch layouts for clients, which I find speeds up the design process.\r\n\r\nI would love to bring my enthusiasm for planting to Terraform. Thank you for considering my application.\r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\nAmara Dlamini</div>\r\n",
