    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 196–200 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">GearUp Cycles Opens Downtown Service Hub\r\n\r\nGearUp Cycles, the bicycle service chain, opened its newest hub on Weaver Street this week — its largest yet and the first to stay open until 8 P.M. on weekdays for after-work repairs. The hub offers same-day tune-ups, a wide parts inventory, and a comfortable waiting lounge with free coffee.\r\n\r\nTo celebrate, GearUp is offering a free safety check with any repair through the end of the month. The chain also launched a mobile app that lets customers book repair slots in advance and earn a free tune-up for every six services.\r\n\r\n&quot;Riders told us they couldn&#x27;t get to a shop before it closed after work,&quot; said service manager Delia Frost. &quot;The later hours and the app are our answer to that.&quot;</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">★★★☆☆  Reviewed by Marcus O.\r\n\r\nI brought my commuter bike to the new Weaver Street hub on a weekday evening, mainly because it stays open late — a real lifesaver since I finish work at six. The tune-up was quick and well done, and the free coffee in the lounge was a nice touch.\r\n\r\nMy frustration was the app. I tried to book my slot in advance, but it kept freezing at the confirmation screen, and my service count never updated toward the free tune-up. I ended up booking by phone instead. The staff were apologetic and squeezed me in. I&#x27;ll be back for the hours and the work, but the app needs fixing.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: marcus.o@mail.com\r\nFrom: d.frost@gearupcycles.com\r\nSubject: Thank you for your feedback\r\nDate: June 27\r\n\r\nDear Marcus,\r\n\r\nThank you for visiting our Weaver Street hub and for taking the time to review it. I&#x27;m glad the later hours and the quick tune-up worked for you, but I&#x27;m sorry the app caused trouble.\r\n\r\nOur development team has fixed the freezing problem you described at the confirmation screen, and the service-count feature is now recording correctly. As an apology, I&#x27;ve added credit for one free tune-up to your account, which you&#x27;ll see the next time you log in.\r\n\r\nFeedback like yours is genuinely helpful and makes us better. I hope to see you again soon.\r\n\r\nWarm regards,\r\nDelia Frost\r\nService Manager, GearUp Cycles</div>\r\n",
