    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 153–155 refer to the following Email.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: Siobhan Gallagher, Hotel Marisco\r\nFrom: Piotr Wierzbicki, Brantwood Furniture Works\r\nDate: April 2\r\nSubject: Order 5521 (bedside tables)\r\n\r\nDear Ms. Gallagher,\r\n\r\nI am writing about your order of 140 bedside tables for the guest rooms at the Hotel Marisco. Our supplier of walnut veneer has just informed us that its next shipment will reach our factory two weeks later than planned. As a result, we will not be able to complete the full order by your requested delivery date of May 4.\r\n\r\nWe can, however, deliver 80 tables on May 4 as scheduled, with the remaining 60 following by May 18. Since I understand that your renovation is proceeding one floor at a time, I hope this arrangement will still suit your timeline. Please let me know by Friday which floors should receive the first delivery so that our warehouse can label the cartons accordingly.\r\n\r\nTo make up for the inconvenience, there will be no charge for the second delivery. I apologize for this change and thank you for your understanding.\r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\nPiotr Wierzbicki\r\nCustomer Accounts</div>\r\n",
