    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 156–158 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.lockwellparcel.com/lockers\r\n\r\nLockwell Parcel | Collect at a Locker\r\n\r\nNot at home during the day? Have your parcels delivered to one of our 300 self-service lockers in train stations, supermarkets, and community centers across the region. Lockers are open 24 hours a day, so you can pick up your items whenever it suits you.\r\n\r\nHow It Works\r\n1. When shopping online, choose &quot;Lockwell Locker&quot; as your delivery option and select a location.\r\n2. As soon as your parcel has been placed in a locker, we will send you a six-digit code by text message.\r\n3. Enter the code on the locker&#x27;s touch screen, and the door will open.\r\n\r\nCollection Time\r\nParcels are held for five days. Any parcel that has not been collected by the end of the fifth day will be returned to the sender, who may charge a fee to send it again. Lockers accept parcels up to 60 centimeters on the longest side and up to 15 kilograms in weight.\r\n\r\nFor Businesses\r\nOur new Locker Plus plan allows small online sellers to drop off up to 50 outgoing parcels a day at any locker location. Visit our Business page to learn more.</div>\r\n",
