    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 159–161 refer to the following Memo.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">MEMORANDUM\r\n\r\nTo: All Production Staff, Wardle Glassworks\r\nFrom: Mattias Ekholm, Plant Manager\r\nDate: August 3\r\nRe: Furnace 2 maintenance week\r\n\r\nAs announced at last month&#x27;s staff meeting, Furnace 2 will be shut down from Monday, August 17, to Friday, August 21, so that its worn interior lining can be replaced. During this period, the bottle line that the furnace supplies will not operate.\r\n\r\nEmployees who normally work on the bottle line will be given other duties that week. Some will assist our contractor, Arkell Refractory Services, with the relining work, while others will join the packing team or complete their annual safety refresher course. Supervisors will post individual assignments on the notice board by August 10.\r\n\r\nPlease also note that the north gate on Bellfield Road will be closed for the entire week, as the contractor will be using the yard behind it to store equipment and materials. Staff who normally use that gate should enter through the main entrance on Wardle Way instead.\r\n\r\nIf you have any questions, please speak to your shift supervisor.</div>\r\n",
