    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 162–164 refer to the following Press release.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\r\nMarch 18\r\nContact: Margaux Lefèvre, Communications Director, (555) 0172\r\n\r\nSaltmere Hotels to Welcome Guests&#x27; Dogs\r\n\r\nSaltmere Hotels announced today that, beginning June 1, guests traveling with dogs will be welcome at all fourteen of its properties. — [1] —. The decision follows a survey in which nearly a third of the company&#x27;s regular guests said they had stayed elsewhere because they could not bring their pets.\r\n\r\nDogs will be allowed only in designated rooms on the first two floors of each hotel, close to the exits. — [2] —. Each of these rooms will be supplied with a dog bed, food and water bowls, and a small welcome package of treats. A cleaning fee of $30 per stay will apply.\r\n\r\nSaltmere has also partnered with local dog-walking businesses in every city where it operates, so guests attending meetings or dining out can arrange a walk through the front desk. — [3] —.\r\n\r\n&quot;Many of our guests consider their dogs part of the family,&quot; said Saltmere chief executive Adebayo Fashola. &quot;We want both of them to feel at home with us.&quot; — [4] —. Pet-friendly rooms can be reserved on the Saltmere website or by telephone.</div>\r\n",
