    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 168–171 refer to the following Online chat discussion.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Livia Bellini (9:02 A.M.): Morning, everyone. Harlan Marine has asked whether we could ship their 6,000 hatch hinges on the 14th instead of the 21st. They&#x27;ve moved up the launch of their new sailboat.\r\nSelim Demir (9:04 A.M.): Line 2 is spoken for through the 12th.\r\nLivia Bellini (9:05 A.M.): By the Fairbairn order?\r\nSelim Demir (9:05 A.M.): Right, and that one can&#x27;t slip. They&#x27;re our biggest customer.\r\nKarthik Iyer (9:06 A.M.): Also keep in mind that every batch needs two days in inspection before it can leave the building.\r\nLivia Bellini (9:08 A.M.): What if we sent part of the order on the 14th and the rest on the 21st? They mainly need enough hinges for the first few boats.\r\nSelim Demir (9:09 A.M.): That could work. If I add a Saturday shift on the 7th, we could have about 2,500 hinges ready for inspection by Monday the 9th.\r\nKarthik Iyer (9:10 A.M.): Then my team can have them cleared by the 11th.\r\nEwa Szymańska (9:12 A.M.): Just confirm the final quantity with me by Thursday. The carrier needs two days&#x27; notice to add a pickup.\r\nLivia Bellini (9:13 A.M.): Great. I&#x27;ll check with Harlan Marine whether 2,500 will be enough and get back to you all before lunch.</div>\r\n",
