    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 176–180 refer to the following Article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Skerry Line to Add Overnight Freight Sailing\r\n\r\nBusinesses on Kilbrannan Island will soon have a faster way to get their goods to the mainland. Beginning on Monday, May 4, Skerry Line will operate a freight-only sailing from Kilbrannan to the port of Ardmore every night except Sunday. The ship will leave at 11:30 P.M. and arrive at 4:00 A.M., in time for goods to reach the mainland&#x27;s early-morning markets and the Ardmore rail freight terminal.\r\n\r\nAt present, all freight travels on Skerry Line&#x27;s three daily passenger ferries. During the busy summer months, these ferries are often full, and trucks are sometimes left on the pier to wait for the next sailing.\r\n\r\nThe freight ship can carry up to 40 trucks and trailers. Businesses that book space on the same night each week for at least three months will receive a 15 percent discount. All bookings must be made at least 48 hours before departure, either online or at the freight office on Kilbrannan Pier.\r\n\r\n&quot;Island producers have been asking for a service like this for years,&quot; said Skerry Line freight manager Aurelio Batista.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: freight@skerryline.com\r\nFrom: Fenella Rourke, Kilbrannan Woolen Mill\r\nDate: April 20\r\nSubject: Bookings on the new freight sailing\r\n\r\nHello,\r\n\r\nI read about your new overnight sailing in last week&#x27;s Island Gazette, and I would like to book space for our delivery truck. At present, our blankets and knitwear travel on the 6:00 P.M. passenger ferry, but last summer our truck was left behind three times, and we missed deliveries to several of our mainland customers as a result.\r\n\r\nWe would like to reserve space for one truck every Tuesday and Thursday night from May 5 until the end of September. As this will be a regular weekly booking, I assume we will qualify for the discount mentioned in the article. In December, our busiest month, we would also like to add a sailing on Sunday nights.\r\n\r\nFinally, could you tell me whether our driver may travel with the truck, or whether he should collect it in Ardmore the next morning?\r\n\r\nBest regards,\r\nFenella Rourke\r\nLogistics Coordinator</div>\r\n",
