    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 181–185 refer to the following Letter.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Brackwater District Council\r\nEconomic Development Office\r\n45 Guildhall Square, Brackwater\r\n\r\nFebruary 2\r\n\r\nDear Business Owner,\r\n\r\nWe are pleased to announce the return of the Storefront Improvement Grant, which helps small businesses in the Old Market area improve the outside of their premises. Last year, the program funded 32 projects, from new signs to restored windows, and the results can be seen throughout the district.\r\n\r\nThis year, grants will cover 50 percent of eligible costs, up to a maximum of $4,000 per business. Eligible projects include signs, exterior lighting, awnings, painting, and window or door repairs. Interior work and equipment purchases are not eligible.\r\n\r\nTo apply, complete the enclosed form and return it with written quotes from two licensed contractors and at least one photograph of your current storefront. Applications must be received by March 15. Because funds are limited, grants will be awarded in the order in which complete applications are received.\r\n\r\nIf you have any questions, please contact Vikram Sethi at (555) 0127.\r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\nDefne Arslan\r\nDirector of Economic Development</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">STOREFRONT IMPROVEMENT GRANT: APPLICATION FORM\r\nBrackwater District Council, Economic Development Office\r\n\r\nBusiness name: The Juniper Tearoom\r\nOwner: Joaquín Herrera\r\nBusiness address: 17 Cooper&#x27;s Row, Old Market, Brackwater\r\nTelephone: (555) 0164\r\n\r\nDescription of project: Replace the faded wooden sign above the entrance, install two outdoor wall lamps, and repaint the front of the building.\r\n\r\nEstimated total cost: $9,600\r\n\r\nDocuments enclosed (check all that apply):\r\n[X] Contractor quote (Lindell &amp; Daughters Signs)\r\n[ ] Second contractor quote\r\n[X] Photograph(s) of current storefront\r\n\r\nDate: February 20\r\nSignature: Joaquín Herrera</div>\r\n",
