    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 186–190 refer to the following Catalog page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">TORSVIK SHELVING SYSTEMS\r\nProduct Catalog, Page 12: Steel Storage Shelving\r\n\r\nAll Torsvik units are manufactured at our plant in Rennick from recycled steel and come with a ten-year warranty. Orders over $1,000 ship free within seven business days.\r\n\r\nModel | Size (W x D x H) | Shelves | Maximum load per shelf | Price\r\nHS-200 | 120 x 45 x 180 cm | 4 | 150 kg | $129\r\nHS-300 | 120 x 60 x 200 cm | 5 | 250 kg | $189\r\nHS-400 | 150 x 60 x 200 cm | 5 | 350 kg | $249\r\nHS-500 | 180 x 75 x 240 cm | 6 | 500 kg | $339\r\n\r\nAssembly service is available in most areas for $35 per unit. Registered charities receive 10 percent off the price of all shelving units. To order, contact our sales team at orders@torsvikshelving.com.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">PURCHASE ORDER No. 1187\r\nRavelston Community Food Bank, 9 Wharf Street, Ravelston\r\nDate: June 2\r\nSupplier: Torsvik Shelving Systems\r\n\r\nItem | Quantity | Unit price | Amount\r\nHS-400 shelving unit | 6 | $249 | $1,494\r\nHS-200 shelving unit | 4 | $129 | $516\r\nAssembly service | 10 | $35 | $350\r\nSubtotal: $2,360\r\nCharity discount (10% of shelving): -$201\r\nOrder total: $2,159\r\n\r\nRequested delivery date: June 20\r\nNote: The larger units will hold heavy canned goods, so each of their shelves must support at least 300 kg.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Nkechi Adeyinka (10:12 A.M.): Lars from Torsvik just called about our shelving order. The HS-400 is out of stock until early July.\r\nMalia Fonoti (10:14 A.M.): July? We open the new warehouse on June 22. Did he offer any alternatives?\r\nNkechi Adeyinka (10:15 A.M.): Two. They can send HS-300 units right away, or upgrade us to the HS-500 at no extra cost and deliver by June 18.\r\nMalia Fonoti (10:17 A.M.): The HS-300 won&#x27;t work for the canned goods. And I measured the storage room yesterday. The ceiling is only 2.3 meters high under the beams.\r\nNkechi Adeyinka (10:18 A.M.): Then the upgrade is out, too. I&#x27;ll ask Lars to send the HS-200 units now and the rest as soon as they&#x27;re available.\r\nMalia Fonoti (10:20 A.M.): Good plan. We can use the smaller units for dry goods in the meantime.</div>\r\n",
