    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 191–195 refer to the following Schedule.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">HAVERLY TOWNSHIP SANITATION DEPARTMENT\r\nHoliday Collection Schedule: Week of October 12\r\n\r\nBecause of the Harvest Day holiday on Monday, October 12, trash and recycling collection in every zone will take place one day later than usual that week. Regular schedules resume on Monday, October 19.\r\n\r\nZone | Neighborhood | Regular day | Week of October 12\r\nA | North End | Monday | Tuesday\r\nB | Canal Side | Tuesday | Wednesday\r\nC | Mill Green | Wednesday | Thursday\r\nD | Stonecroft | Thursday | Friday\r\nE | Westfield | Friday | Saturday\r\n\r\nReminders: Bins must be at the curb by 7:00 A.M. with their lids fully closed. Extra cardboard that does not fit in your bin may be dropped off free of charge at the Cobb Lane Recycling Center, which is open Tuesday through Saturday from 8:00 A.M. to 4:00 P.M.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">HAVERLY TOWNSHIP SANITATION DEPARTMENT\r\nCollection Notice\r\n\r\nAddress: 52 Orchard Crescent\r\nDate: October 14\r\n\r\nWe&#x27;re sorry, but we could not empty your recycling bin today for the reason checked below:\r\n[ ] Bin was not at the curb by 7:00 A.M.\r\n[X] Lid was not fully closed\r\n[ ] Bin contained items that cannot be recycled\r\n[ ] Bin was too heavy to lift safely\r\n\r\nPlease correct the problem before your next collection day. Questions? Call (555) 0110.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: sanitation@haverlytownship.gov\r\nFrom: Takumi Hayashi\r\nDate: October 15\r\nSubject: Recycling at 52 Orchard Crescent\r\n\r\nHello,\r\n\r\nYesterday I found a notice on my recycling bin explaining that it could not be emptied because the lid was not closed. That was fair. We had just received a delivery of new furniture, and the packaging would not fit inside the bin.\r\n\r\nI have since flattened the boxes, but there is still far more cardboard than the bin can hold, so I would like to take it to the recycling center myself. Since I work long hours during the week, the weekend would be best for me. Could you tell me whether I need to bring proof that I live in the township?\r\n\r\nAlso, one of my neighbors mentioned that collection on our street will move to a different day next year. Is that correct?\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\nTakumi Hayashi</div>\r\n",
