    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 196–200 refer to the following Web page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">www.aldmoorhotel.com/lost-and-found\r\n\r\nThe Aldmoor Hotel | Lost and Found\r\n\r\nDid you leave something behind? Items found in guest rooms and public areas are recorded by our housekeeping team and stored securely for 60 days. Valuable items, such as jewelry, laptops, and passports, are kept in the hotel safe. Items that are not claimed within 60 days are donated to local charities.\r\n\r\nTo report a missing item, please e-mail lostandfound@aldmoorhotel.com with a description of the item, the dates of your stay, and where you think you left it. We will reply within two business days.\r\n\r\nItems may be collected in person at the front desk at any time, or we can send them to you by courier. Shipping charges are billed to the guest when the parcel is sent:\r\n• Within the country: $15 (up to 2 kg) or $25 (over 2 kg)\r\n• International: $40 (up to 2 kg) or $65 (over 2 kg)</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: lostandfound@aldmoorhotel.com\r\nFrom: Francesca Moretti\r\nDate: March 9\r\nSubject: Items left behind\r\n\r\nHello,\r\n\r\nI stayed at the Aldmoor from March 3 to 6 in Room 512, and I believe I left two items behind. The first is a phone charger with a white cable, which I think is still plugged in beside the bed. The second is a gray wool scarf that I wore to dinner in your restaurant on the evening of March 5.\r\n\r\nCould you please send whatever you find to my home address, 14 Fairlie Row, Dunstan Bay? I am happy to pay the shipping charges. Alternatively, I will be back in the city for the Westmarch Tourism Forum in April, so I could also pick the items up then.\r\n\r\nThank you for your help.\r\n\r\nFrancesca Moretti</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">To: Francesca Moretti\r\nFrom: Noriko Ishikawa, Housekeeping Manager\r\nDate: March 10\r\nSubject: RE: Items left behind\r\n\r\nDear Ms. Moretti,\r\n\r\nThank you for contacting us. I am pleased to report that our housekeeping staff found your phone charger when they cleaned your room on March 6. Unfortunately, we have not been able to locate your scarf. I have checked with the staff who worked on the evening of March 5, and no scarf was turned in. We will contact you right away if it is found.\r\n\r\nWe can send the charger to you this week, and a fee of $15 will be charged to the credit card you used during your stay. However, since you mentioned that you will be returning to the city soon, you may prefer to collect it from the front desk then and avoid the charge. Please let me know which option you would like.\r\n\r\nBest regards,\r\nNoriko Ishikawa</div>\r\n",
