    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 135–138 refer to the following e-mail.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Ms. Suzuki,\r\nThank you for choosing Threadworks Tailoring for your custom suit. I am writing to let you know that the charcoal wool fabric you selected is\r\n135\r\nout of stock at our supplier in Leeds. The supplier expects to receive a new shipment in about three weeks.\r\n136\r\n, your suit would be ready for collection on 20 June instead of 1 June as originally planned.\r\nIf this delay is inconvenient, we would be happy to make your suit from a similar fabric produced by another mill.\r\n137\r\nEach of them has the same weight and finish as your original choice, and there would be no change in price.\r\nPlease let me know which option you\r\n138\r\nby Friday so that we can proceed with your order.\r\nBest regards,\r\nLiam O’Connell\r\nThreadworks Tailoring</div>\r\n",
