    "</h2>\r\n<div class=\"dirs\"><b>Directions:</b> In this part you will read a selection of texts, such as magazine and newspaper articles, e-mails, and instant messages. Each text or set of texts is followed by several questions. Select the best answer for each question and mark the letter (A), (B), (C), or (D) on your answer sheet.</div>\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 147–148 refer to the following text-message-chain.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Diego Ramírez 9:12 A.M.: Hi Aisha, I’m at the Lakeview Convention Center setting up our booth. The banners haven’t turned up.\r\nAisha Rahman 9:14 A.M.: That’s strange. The print shop promised they’d be delivered straight to the loading dock this morning.\r\nDiego Ramírez 9:15 A.M.: I asked the dock manager. Nothing has come in under our company name.\r\nAisha Rahman 9:17 A.M.: Let me call the print shop now.\r\nAisha Rahman 9:26 A.M.: OK, their driver is stuck in traffic on the ring road. He should be with you by 10:30.\r\nDiego Ramírez 9:27 A.M.: The doors open to the public at 11:00.\r\nAisha Rahman 9:28 A.M.: I know it’s tight. Could you get the tables and product samples arranged in the meantime?\r\nDiego Ramírez 9:29 A.M.: Already on it.</div>\r\n",
