    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 151–152 refer to the following press-release.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Quillsoft Launches ShiftMate Scheduling App</span>TORONTO (2 September) — Quillsoft Inc. today announced the launch of ShiftMate, a scheduling application designed for restaurants, retail stores, and other small businesses with hourly staff. ShiftMate allows managers to build weekly schedules in minutes and lets employees exchange shifts with coworkers directly from their phones, subject to a manager’s approval.\r\n“Small business owners told us they were spending up to six hours a week on staff schedules,” said Quillsoft CEO Daniel Hoffmann. “ShiftMate reduces that time dramatically.”\r\nThe app was tested for eight months by more than 300 businesses across Canada before its public release. ShiftMate is free for teams of up to ten employees; larger teams pay $3 per employee per month. It is available now for both major mobile platforms, and a desktop version is planned for early next year.</div>\r\n",
    {
      "slot": "question.50"
