      "slot": "question.53"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 155–157 refer to the following review.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Old Town Food Walk, Lisbon ★★★★☆</span>My colleagues and I booked this three-hour tour on the last evening of a week-long business trip, and it turned out to be the highlight of our stay. Our guide, Rui, met us at the fountain in Praça da Figueira at exactly 6:00 P.M. and led us to six family-run establishments, where we sampled everything from grilled sardines to custard tarts. Rui clearly knew the owners personally, and his stories about the history of each neighborhood made the walks between stops go by quickly.\r\nMy only complaint concerns the booking information. The company’s Web site stated that drinks were included, but at two of the stops we had to pay for our own beverages. When I e-mailed the company afterward, a representative apologized and explained that the site had not been updated since the tour changed its menu. She offered me a 20 percent discount on a future tour, which was a kind gesture, although I am not sure when I will next be in Lisbon.\r\nA word of advice: wear comfortable shoes, as some of the streets are steep and cobbled. I would recommend this tour to anyone visiting the city.</div>\r\n",
