    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 158–160 refer to the following article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Skyreach Air to Expand Regional Network</span>PERTH (18 August) — Skyreach Air, a regional carrier based in Perth, will add four new routes to its network beginning in November, the airline announced on Monday. The new services will connect Perth with Geraldton, Esperance, Broome, and Kalgoorlie, towns that until now have been served mainly by small charter operators.\r\nTo operate the routes, Skyreach has leased three turboprop aircraft, each seating 72 passengers. The airline is also hiring 40 new staff members, including pilots, cabin crew, and ground personnel. According to chief executive Olivia Brennan, most of the new ground staff will work at the regional airports rather than in Perth.\r\n“Residents of these communities have been asking for affordable, scheduled flights for years,” Ms. Brennan said. “Many of them travel to Perth regularly for business meetings, university classes, and family visits.”\r\nIntroductory fares start at $129 one way and will go on sale on the airline’s Web site on 1 September. Flights to Broome will run daily, while the other three routes will operate four times a week.</div>\r\n",
