    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 164–167 refer to the following online-chat-discussion.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Mei Lin Zhou 2:03 P.M.: Quick update on the Harborview retreat for Fenwick Logistics. The client just told me they’ll have 85 attendees, not 60.\r\nSamuel Adeyemi 2:04 P.M.: That’s a big jump. The Tern Room at the Harborview seats 70 at most.\r\nClara Novak 2:05 P.M.: The Osprey Hall is free that weekend — I checked the venue calendar this morning. It holds 120.\r\nMei Lin Zhou 2:06 P.M.: Is the price very different?\r\nClara Novak 2:08 P.M.: It’s about $900 more for the two days, but the rate includes a projector and sound system. We were going to rent those separately for around $600.\r\nRajesh Iyer 2:09 P.M.: So the real difference is only about $300. I’d say that’s a no-brainer.\r\nMei Lin Zhou 2:10 P.M.: Agreed. I’ll need the client’s approval first, though, since it goes over the budget we quoted them.\r\nSamuel Adeyemi 2:11 P.M.: What about lunches? The catering order was for 60 people.\r\nRajesh Iyer 2:12 P.M.: I’ll call Bayleaf Catering and find out whether they can serve 85 with the same menu.\r\nMei Lin Zhou 2:13 P.M.: Thanks, Rajesh. Clara, could you put a hold on the Osprey Hall until Friday?\r\nClara Novak 2:14 P.M.: Will do.</div>\r\n",
