    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 172–175 refer to the following advertisement.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Harbor Point Coworking — Your Office by the Water</span>Tired of working from your kitchen table?\r\n[1]\r\nHarbor Point Coworking offers bright, fully furnished workspaces in the restored Customs House on Wharf Street, just a five-minute walk from the ferry terminal.\r\nChoose the plan that suits you: Flex Desk ($180/month) — use any open desk, Monday to Friday, 8:00 A.M. to 7:00 P.M. Dedicated Desk ($320/month) — your own desk and locking cabinet, with 24-hour access. Private Office (from $950/month) — lockable offices for teams of two to six people.\r\n[2]\r\nAll plans include high-speed Internet, printing, and unlimited coffee and tea.\r\nMembers may also book one of our two meeting rooms, each seating up to twelve people, for $25 per hour.\r\n[3]\r\nFlex Desk members receive three hours of free meeting-room time every month.\r\nSign up before 31 January and pay only half price for your first month.\r\n[4]\r\nVisit harborpointcowork.com or stop by for a free one-day trial pass.</div>\r\n",
