    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 176–180 refer to the following e-mail.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Dr. Haidari,\r\nThank you again for agreeing to speak at this year’s International Pharmaceutical Packaging Forum in Vienna. Your session, “Reducing Plastic in Blister Packs,” is scheduled for Thursday, 22 May, at 10:30 A.M. in Hall B. Each speaker is allotted 40 minutes, including 10 minutes for questions from the audience.\r\nAs agreed, the Forum will cover your accommodation for the nights of 21 and 22 May at the Hotel Lindenhof, a short walk from the conference center. Speakers are responsible for booking their own flights; however, we will reimburse economy-class airfare of up to €400 upon receipt of your ticket invoice.\r\nPlease send your presentation slides to me by 12 May so that our technical team can load them onto the computer in the hall. If you require any additional equipment, let me know as soon as possible.\r\nFinally, all speakers are warmly invited to the opening reception, which will be held at the conference center on the evening of 21 May from 7:00 to 9:00 P.M. Please tell me by 12 May whether you plan to attend.\r\nBest regards,\r\nJonas Becker\r\nSpeaker Coordinator</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Mr. Becker,\r\nThank you for the details. I have booked my flights and attached the invoice; the round-trip economy fare came to €465. I understand that the Forum’s contribution is limited.\r\nI have one request. My colleague Tobias Lund, who led the laboratory testing described in my presentation, will also be attending the Forum. Would it be possible for him to join me on stage for the question period? He can answer technical questions far better than I can. He has already registered as a regular attendee, so he has his own conference pass.\r\nIn addition, I plan to show a short video clip during my talk, so I will need speakers connected to the hall computer. My slides will reach you before your deadline. Unfortunately, because of a prior commitment, I will not be able to arrive in Vienna until the evening before my session. I am afraid I will probably miss most of the opening reception as a result, but I would be glad to join if my flight lands on time.\r\nKind regards,\r\nFarida Haidari</div>\r\n",
