    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 186–190 refer to the following memo.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">The second-quarter planning meeting will be held on Wednesday, 19 March, from 9:00 A.M. to 12:00 P.M. in Conference Room 4. Please note that this is a change from our usual location, as the boardroom is being repainted that week. Coffee and tea will be available in the room from 8:45 A.M.\r\nEach department head should be prepared to give a brief update on first-quarter results. In addition, Paulo Mendes from our Singapore facility will join us by video call to discuss the new packaging line that will be installed there in May. Because of the time difference, his presentation has been placed in the first slot after the break. He will also answer questions about the equipment suppliers chosen for the project.\r\nThe draft agenda is attached. If you would like to add or change an item, please contact my assistant, Yara Haddad, by 14 March. Department heads who cannot attend in person should arrange for a deputy to present their department’s information.\r\nLunch will be served in the staff dining room immediately after the meeting. Please also let Yara know by 14 March if you have any dietary requirements.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Q2 Planning Meeting — Draft Agenda (Wednesday, 19 March, Conference Room 4)</span>Agenda\r\n· Text 2 of 3\r\nQ2 Planning Meeting — Draft Agenda (Wednesday, 19 March, Conference Room 4)\r\nTime\r\nItem\r\nPresenter\r\n9:00–9:15\r\nWelcome and overview\r\nHelena Sørensen\r\n9:15–10:00\r\nQ1 results by department\r\nDepartment heads\r\n10:00–10:30\r\nSupplier contract renewals\r\nIbrahim Kaya, Purchasing\r\n10:30–10:45\r\nBreak\r\n—\r\n10:45–11:15\r\nSingapore packaging line\r\nPaulo Mendes (video call)\r\n11:15–11:45\r\nWorkplace safety training plan\r\nGrace Adjei, Human Resources\r\n11:45–12:00\r\nQuestions and closing remarks\r\nHelena Sørensen\r\nEach department head will have about five minutes for his or her Q1 update. Presenters who wish to show slides should send them to Yara Haddad by 17 March.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Hi Yara,\r\nI have just learned that I need to be at our supplier’s plant in Gdańsk on 19 March to sign the final contracts, so I will not be able to attend the planning meeting. My deputy, Lena Fischer, has agreed to present the contract renewals in my place. Lena has worked on these negotiations with me since January, so she is fully familiar with the details, and I will send her my notes and the latest supplier figures by Friday. Could you please update the presenter’s name on the agenda?\r\nLena also pointed out that the contract discussion may need more than the 30 minutes currently scheduled, since two of our largest suppliers have proposed significant price increases. Would you ask Ms. Sørensen whether the item could be extended, perhaps by shortening the closing remarks? I will be back in the office on Monday, 24 March, if she would like to discuss the contracts with me directly.\r\nThanks,\r\nIbrahim</div>\r\n",
