    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 191–195 refer to the following article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Express Trains Coming to Northline</span>WESTBRIDGE (4 August) — Commuters on the Northline rail route will soon have a faster option. Beginning Monday, 1 September, Westbridge Regional Transit (WRT) will introduce express trains that stop only at Harlow, Fenton Park, and Central Station, cutting the journey from Harlow to the city center from 58 minutes to 41.\r\nThe express trains will run during the morning and evening rush hours on weekdays only. Regular trains, which stop at all eleven stations on the line, will continue to operate throughout the day.\r\nWRT spokesperson Chidi Okonkwo said the change responds to rapid population growth in Harlow, where several large housing developments have been completed over the past two years. “Passenger numbers at Harlow station have doubled since 2023,” he said.\r\nTickets for express trains will cost the same as those for regular service. In addition, WRT will launch a new monthly pass priced at $140, allowing unlimited travel on both express and regular trains. Riders who buy the pass before 1 September will receive a 10 percent discount.\r\nThe express service is the first stage of a larger upgrade of the Northline. WRT also plans to expand the car park at Harlow station by 150 spaces by the end of the year and to lengthen the platforms at Fenton Park by 2027 so that longer trains can be used.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Hello,\r\nI live in Harlow and work in an office near Central Station. My workday begins at 8:15 A.M. At the moment, I take the 6:55 regular train, which gets me there on time but means getting up very early. I was delighted to read about the new express service in the newspaper, and several of my neighbors are also planning to switch to it.\r\nI have two questions. First, will I be allowed to bring my folding bicycle on express trains, as I currently do on regular trains? Second, I bought a regular monthly ticket on 1 August that is valid until the end of this month. If I purchase the new pass for September today, will I still receive the discount?\r\nThank you,\r\nRosa Villanueva</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Northline Express — Weekday Morning Timetable (from 1 September)</span>Evening express trains depart Central Station for Harlow at 5:10, 5:40, 6:10, and 6:40 P.M. Express trains do not stop at Millbrook, Ashford Road, or any other intermediate station. Tickets and monthly passes can be purchased from station ticket machines or through the WRT mobile app. Times are subject to change; please check wrt-transit.com for the latest information.</div>\r\n",
