    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 135–138 refer to the following article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Greenvale Cooperative to Expand Drone Program</span>GREENVALE — The Greenvale Farmers’ Cooperative announced on Tuesday that it will expand its crop-monitoring program to all 140 member farms by next spring. Since the pilot program began two years ago, small drones\r\n135\r\nfields of wheat and barley on twelve farms, photographing the crops once a week.\r\nThe images help farmers identify areas that need water or fertilizer before problems become visible from the ground.\r\n136\r\n, participating farms reduced their fertilizer use by an average of 18 percent last season.\r\nThe expansion will be funded in part by a grant from the provincial agriculture ministry. Members will also pay a small annual fee to cover the\r\n137\r\nof the equipment, including repairs and replacement batteries.\r\nCooperative director Imani Wekesa said the program has been popular with growers.\r\n138</div>\r\n",
