    "</h2>\r\n<div class=\"dirs\"><b>Directions:</b> In this part you will read a selection of texts, such as magazine and newspaper articles, e-mails, and instant messages. Each text or set of texts is followed by several questions. Select the best answer for each question and mark the letter (A), (B), (C), or (D) on your answer sheet.</div>\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 147–148 refer to the following text-message-chain.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Lucía Ferreyra 2:14 P.M.: Hi Dmitri. The owner of the blue hatchback just called again. She wants to know if her car will be ready by the end of the day.\r\nDmitri Volkov 2:16 P.M.: Not yet. We’re still waiting for the brake pads from Hollins Auto Parts. They were supposed to be delivered this morning.\r\nLucía Ferreyra 2:17 P.M.: She’s leaving on a business trip early tomorrow, so she really needs it tonight. Is there anything we can do?\r\nDmitri Volkov 2:19 P.M.: Kofi is driving to their warehouse right now.\r\nLucía Ferreyra 2:20 P.M.: That’s a relief. How long will the job take once he’s back?\r\nDmitri Volkov 2:21 P.M.: About an hour and a half. She should be able to pick it up by six.\r\nLucía Ferreyra 2:22 P.M.: Perfect. I’ll call her back and let her know.</div>\r\n",
