    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 151–152 refer to the following article.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Telvaro Brings Coverage to Highland Villages</span>SAN MIGUEL DE LOS ALTOS — Telvaro Communications has completed the installation of fourteen new cell towers in the Altos highlands, bringing reliable mobile service to more than thirty villages for the first time. Until now, many residents had to drive up to 40 kilometers to make a phone call or send a message.\r\nThe project, which cost an estimated $22 million, was partly funded by a national program that encourages companies to extend service to remote communities. Telvaro spokesperson Renata Iturbide said the company chose the area because of its fast-growing tourism industry. “Visitors come for the hiking trails and hot springs, and they expect to stay connected,” she explained.\r\nLocal business owners welcome the change. Mateo Quilca, who runs a small guesthouse in the village of Pumaqaqa, says some guests have left early in the past because they could not work remotely. “Now I can finally advertise high-speed service,” he said.\r\nTelvaro plans to install six additional towers in the neighboring Condor Valley next year.</div>\r\n",
