    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 172–175 refer to the following instructions.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">SunVessa P300 Portable Power Station — Getting Started</span>Thank you for purchasing the SunVessa P300. This portable battery can power laptops, small appliances, and camping lights for up to 12 hours on a single charge.\r\n[1]\r\nCharging: Before first use, charge the unit fully. It can be charged from a standard wall outlet (about 6 hours), a car’s 12-volt socket (about 9 hours), or the SunVessa folding solar panel, sold separately (about 8 hours in direct sunlight).\r\n[2]\r\nThe display on the front shows the remaining battery level as a percentage.\r\nUse: Press and hold the power button for three seconds to turn the unit on. Do not connect devices that require more than 300 watts, such as hair dryers or electric kettles.\r\n[3]\r\nIf the unit is overloaded, it will shut off automatically to protect the battery.\r\nStorage: When not in use, store the P300 in a cool, dry place and recharge it at least once every three months.\r\n[4]\r\nYour P300 is covered by a two-year warranty when registered at www.sunvessa.com within 30 days of purchase.</div>\r\n",
