    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 176–180 refer to the following e-mail.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Reservations Team,\r\nI am writing on behalf of Meridia Journeys to request rooms for a tour group visiting Porto from 12 to 15 May. The group consists of 22 travelers and one tour guide, so we would need 11 double rooms and one single room for three nights.\r\nOur travelers will spend their days on excursions to the Douro Valley and will therefore need breakfast only. However, we would like to hold a private welcome dinner for the whole group on the evening of our arrival. Could you tell me whether your restaurant can accommodate a group of this size, and send me a sample set menu?\r\nFinally, several of our travelers have difficulty with stairs, so rooms on lower floors or near an elevator would be greatly appreciated.\r\nI look forward to your reply.\r\nBest regards,\r\nOriane Vasseur\r\nTour Coordinator, Meridia Journeys</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Ms. Vasseur,\r\nThank you for considering Hotel Miradouro. I am happy to confirm that we can offer 11 double rooms and one single room for the nights of 12, 13, and 14 May. Our group rate is €118 per night for each double room and €92 per night for the single room, breakfast included.\r\nUnfortunately, our restaurant has been booked for a private event on the evening of 12 May. It is, however, available the following evening, and our chef has prepared a three-course set menu at €34 per person, which I have attached. If you would prefer to keep your original date, I would be glad to recommend some nearby restaurants that welcome groups.\r\nThe double rooms we are holding for your group are all on the second and third floors, close to the elevators.\r\nTo secure the booking, please return the signed group contract by 20 March. A deposit of 20 percent of the total will then be charged to your company’s account.\r\nKind regards,\r\nHenrique Valadares\r\nGroup Sales Manager, Hotel Miradouro</div>\r\n",
