    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 191–195 refer to the following notice.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Notice to All Tenants — Brookmere Business Centre</span>Electric vehicle charging stations are being installed in the underground car park. The work will take place from Monday, 3 March, to Friday, 14 March. During this period, Level P2 will be closed.\r\nTenants who normally park on Level P2 may use the Ashgrove Street public car park at no charge. Please collect a free parking voucher from the reception desk on the ground floor before parking there.\r\nWhen the work is complete, sixteen new charging points will be available on Level P2 to all tenants. Charging will cost $0.30 per kilowatt-hour, billed monthly to each tenant company. To register a vehicle for charging access, please contact our facilities manager, Gustavo Pellegrini, at gpellegrini@brookmerebc.com.\r\nContractors will work between 7:00 A.M. and 6:00 P.M., and some noise may be heard on the ground floor. We apologize for any inconvenience and thank you for your patience.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Mr. Pellegrini,\r\nThree employees at Brightwave Telecom Solutions (Suite 410) drive electric cars and would like to register for charging access once the new stations open. I have attached their names and vehicle details. At the moment, they charge their cars at home, but charging at work would be much more convenient for them.\r\nCould you also tell me whether charging points can be reserved in advance? Our sales representatives often return to the office in the afternoon with low batteries and would like to be sure a point is free.\r\nFinally, one of our technicians, Wiremu, usually parks on Level P2, but he was unable to collect a voucher yesterday because the reception desk was closed when he arrived at 7:30 A.M. Is there another way for him to obtain one?\r\nMany thanks,\r\nAroha Tipene\r\nOffice Manager</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Aroha Tipene 8:41 A.M.: Wiremu, Mr. Pellegrini replied. Reception will open at 7:00 A.M. until the construction is finished, so you can pick up a voucher tomorrow morning.\r\nWiremu Harlan 8:43 A.M.: Great, thanks. I’ve had to pay for parking on Ashgrove Street for the last two days. Can I get that money back?\r\nAroha Tipene 8:45 A.M.: Yes. He said to send your receipts to him directly and the building management will reimburse you.\r\nWiremu Harlan 8:46 A.M.: Perfect. Did he say anything about reserving charging points?\r\nAroha Tipene 8:48 A.M.: That won’t be possible, unfortunately. But he thinks sixteen points will be more than enough for the building.\r\nWiremu Harlan 8:50 A.M.: Good to know. I’ll drop off my receipts at his office at lunchtime.\r\nAroha Tipene 8:51 A.M.: Sounds good. And don’t forget to pick up your voucher tomorrow!</div>\r\n",
