    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 196–200 refer to the following brochure.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Wexcombe Hospitality Academy — Autumn Short Courses</span>Whether you manage a boutique hotel or a busy restaurant, our one-day courses help you and your team build practical skills you can use immediately. Since 2015, more than 4,000 hotel and restaurant employees have taken part in our programs. All courses are held at our training center at 40 Quayside Road, Brenton. They run from 9:00 A.M. to 4:30 P.M. and include lunch and all course materials.\r\nGroups of three or more from the same business receive 15 percent off each registration. Registrations must be received at least ten days before the course date. Participants who complete two or more courses this autumn will be awarded a Certificate in Hospitality Operations.\r\nOur instructors are experienced professionals who have worked in leading hotels and restaurants around the world. Class sizes are limited to 16 participants so that everyone receives individual attention. To register, complete the form on the back of this brochure and e-mail it to registrations@wexcombeacademy.com. Payment can be made by credit card or bank transfer.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Wexcombe Hospitality Academy — Registration Form</span>Form\r\n· Text 2 of 3\r\nWexcombe Hospitality Academy — Registration Form\r\nField\r\nDetails\r\nName\r\nThandiwe Mokoena\r\nBusiness\r\nJuniper Lane Inn\r\nPosition\r\nAssistant Manager\r\nE-mail\r\ntmokoena@juniperlaneinn.com\r\nPhone\r\n(041) 555-0138\r\nCourse(s)\r\nHandling Guest Complaints with Confidence; Social Media Marketing for Restaurants\r\nNumber of participants from your business\r\n1\r\nPayment method\r\nCredit card\r\nSpecial requests\r\nVegetarian lunch, please.\r\nHow did you hear about us?\r\nA colleague recommended your courses.\r\nDate submitted\r\n30 September</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Ms. Mokoena,\r\nThank you for registering for two of our autumn short courses. Your payment has been received.\r\nUnfortunately, the instructor for Social Media Marketing for Restaurants is no longer available on 21 October, so that course has been moved to Thursday, 30 October. Please let me know whether you are able to attend on the new date. If not, you may transfer to Wine Service Essentials at no additional cost or receive a full refund for the course. If you keep the new date, the course will be held in the same room and at the same times as originally planned. I apologize for any inconvenience this change may cause.\r\nYour meal request has been noted, and our catering staff will prepare a vegetarian lunch for you on each course day. As a reminder, free parking is available behind the training center, which is also a ten-minute walk from Brenton station. Courses begin promptly at 9:00 A.M., so please plan to arrive a few minutes early.\r\nBest regards,\r\nPieter Duvenhage\r\nRegistrations Coordinator</div>\r\n",
