    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 135–138 refer to the following web-page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Kerrow Valley Farm — Guided Farm Tours</span>Every weekend from June to September, Kerrow Valley Farm opens its gates to visitors\r\n135\r\nwant to see how their food is grown. Our two-hour guided tour takes you through the apple orchards, the dairy barn, and our new greenhouse, where we grow tomatoes and herbs all year round.\r\nOur guides, all of whom live and work on the farm, give\r\n136\r\nexplanations of each stage of production, from planting to packing. Children can help feed the calves, and everyone is invited to taste fresh milk and cheese made on site.\r\nAt the end of the tour, guests are welcome to pick their own strawberries in the fields behind the farmhouse.\r\n137\r\nTickets cost $18 for adults and $9 for children under twelve. Because group sizes are limited to 20 people, we\r\n138\r\nbooking online at least a week before your visit. Tours depart at 10:00 A.M. and 2:00 P.M. from the farm shop.</div>\r\n",
