    "</h2>\r\n<div class=\"dirs\"><b>Directions:</b> In this part you will read a selection of texts, such as magazine and newspaper articles, e-mails, and instant messages. Each text or set of texts is followed by several questions. Select the best answer for each question and mark the letter (A), (B), (C), or (D) on your answer sheet.</div>\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 147–148 refer to the following text-message-chain.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Lorenzo Batista 9:12 A.M.: Hi Priya. The produce delivery just came, but Greenfield Farms sent only half the tomatoes we ordered.\r\nPriya Ramanathan 9:14 A.M.: Again? That’s the second time this month.\r\nLorenzo Batista 9:15 A.M.: We need at least ten kilos for today’s lunch specials.\r\nPriya Ramanathan 9:17 A.M.: I’ll call them and ask for the rest to be sent before 11:00. If they can’t manage it, I’ll pick some up at the wholesale market on my way in.\r\nLorenzo Batista 9:18 A.M.: Sounds good. Should I take the tomato soup off the menu board for now?\r\nPriya Ramanathan 9:19 A.M.: Let’s hold off on that.\r\nLorenzo Batista 9:20 A.M.: OK. I’ll start preparing the other dishes, then.</div>\r\n",
