    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 151–152 refer to the following notice.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Notice to Passengers — Winter Timetable</span>Beginning 1 October, the Port Aldous–Merrow Island ferry will operate on its winter timetable. Departures from Port Aldous will be reduced from eight to five per day, with the first sailing at 7:30 A.M. and the last at 6:00 P.M. The café on the upper deck will be open on weekends only.\r\nBecause the vessel used in winter carries only 24 cars, passengers traveling with vehicles are strongly encouraged to reserve space in advance. Reservations can be made at www.aldousferries.com or at the ticket office in either port. Foot passengers and cyclists do not need a reservation.\r\nMonthly commuter passes purchased before 1 October will remain valid until their expiration date. The summer timetable will return on 1 April.\r\nAldous Island Ferries</div>\r\n",
    {
