    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 153–154 refer to the following survey.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Harborview Suites — Guest Satisfaction Survey</span>Comments: The front desk staff were wonderful. Mr. Adeyemi even arranged a late checkout so that I could return to my room between my final client meeting and my flight home. My only real disappointment was breakfast. By 8:30 most of the hot dishes had run out and were not replaced, which was frustrating when I had early appointments to get to. I will be back in the area in September for a conference and would consider staying here again if this situation improves.</div>\r\n",
    {
      "slot": "question.52"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n",
    {
      "slot": "question.53"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 155–157 refer to the following web-page.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Northbeam Radio 94.7 — Share Your Story on Community Voices</span>Every Sunday at 10:00 A.M., Northbeam Radio airs Community Voices, a half-hour program featuring true stories from listeners across the Tallis Bay region. We are especially interested in stories about local businesses, volunteers, and neighborhood traditions.\r\nHow to submit: Send us a written summary of no more than 300 words using the form below, and include a telephone number so that one of our producers can contact you. Because we receive hundreds of submissions each month, we are able to reply only to those people whose stories are selected for the program.\r\nSelected contributors are invited to our studio on Dace Street to record their story with a producer. Recording sessions usually last about an hour. Contributors who are unable to travel to the studio can record at home using a free recording kit, which we will send to them by mail.\r\nAs a thank-you, every contributor receives a Northbeam Radio travel mug and a digital copy of the finished broadcast.</div>\r\n",
    {
      "slot": "question.54"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n",
    {
      "slot": "question.55"
