    "\r\n\r\n",
    {
      "slot": "question.56"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 158–160 refer to the following instructions.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">GreenRoot Liquid Plant Food — For vegetables, flowers, and houseplants</span>Net contents: 1 liter (makes up to 200 liters of plant food solution)\r\nDirections: Shake well before use. Mix one capful (5 ml) with 1 liter of water. For outdoor plants, apply every two weeks during the growing season (March to September). For houseplants, apply once a month throughout the year. Do not apply to dry soil; water plants lightly before feeding.\r\nStorage: Keep the bottle tightly closed in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight. Do not allow the product to freeze. Keep out of reach of children and pets.\r\nMade by Talvera Agricultural Products, Fresno, California. Questions? Call our gardening helpline at 1-800-555-0192, Monday to Friday, 8:00 A.M. to 5:00 P.M., or visit talvera-agri.com for seasonal planting tips.</div>\r\n",
    {
      "slot": "question.57"
