    {
      "slot": "question.62"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 164–167 refer to the following online-chat-discussion.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Hyun-woo Baek 2:05 P.M.: Quick update: Line 3 is down again. The labeling machine keeps jamming.\r\nAdaeze Nwosu 2:06 P.M.: How long will it take to fix?\r\nHyun-woo Baek 2:07 P.M.: The technician says at least three hours. He has to get a replacement roller from the supplier.\r\nAdaeze Nwosu 2:08 P.M.: That’s a problem. The Merriton order is supposed to go out first thing tomorrow — 4,000 bottles of pasta sauce.\r\nGustavo Pereira 2:10 P.M.: Line 1 finishes its current run at 3:30. We could move the Merriton job over there.\r\nAdaeze Nwosu 2:11 P.M.: Would that delay anything else?\r\nGustavo Pereira 2:12 P.M.: The Holloway order would slip to Thursday, but they don’t need it until next week anyway.\r\nAdaeze Nwosu 2:13 P.M.: Then let’s go with that. Mei, could you let the warehouse know the pallets will be ready later than planned?\r\nMei Rautio 2:15 P.M.: Sure. I’ll message them now, and I’ll ask the evening shift to stay until all the bottles are packed.\r\nHyun-woo Baek 2:16 P.M.: Thanks, everyone. I’ll post again once Line 3 is running.</div>\r\n",
