    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 168–171 refer to the following memo.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">As you know, construction of the new laboratory building on the west side of the Lindgate Pharmaceuticals campus is now complete. I am pleased to announce that the Research and Development department will begin moving into the building on Monday, 8 September.\r\n[1]\r\nThe move will take place in stages over three weeks so that ongoing experiments are disrupted as little as possible.\r\nThe analytical chemistry team will move first, followed by the formulation team during the week of 15 September. The quality control laboratory will remain in its current location until the end of the month, as its new testing equipment has not yet been delivered.\r\n[2]\r\nEach team leader will receive a detailed moving schedule by 29 August. In the meantime, please begin labeling your equipment and supplies using the colored stickers available from the facilities office.\r\n[3]\r\nItems without a label may not be delivered to the correct room.\r\nPlease note that staff will not be able to enter the new building until their security badges have been updated.\r\n[4]\r\nBadges can be updated at the reception desk in the main building on any weekday between 9:00 A.M. and 4:00 P.M. If you have questions about the move, please contact me at extension 4417.</div>\r\n",
    {
      "slot": "question.67"
