    {
      "slot": "question.70"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 172–175 refer to the following press-release.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Castellan Motors Announces New Battery Plant in Rennick</span>DETROIT, 4 June — Castellan Motors today announced plans to build a battery manufacturing plant in Rennick, Ohio, the company’s first facility dedicated to producing batteries for electric vehicles.\r\n[1]\r\nConstruction will begin in October, and the plant is expected to start operating in early 2028.\r\nThe 60,000-square-meter facility will supply batteries for Castellan’s popular Vireo compact SUV as well as two new models that the company plans to introduce over the next three years.\r\n[2]\r\nOnce it reaches full capacity, the plant will employ approximately 1,200 people.\r\n“Rennick offered everything we were looking for: an experienced workforce, excellent rail connections, and strong support from the local government,” said Castellan CEO Martin Oduya.\r\n[3]\r\nThe company is also working with Rennick Community College to develop a training program for future employees. Classes in battery assembly and quality testing will be offered free of charge starting next spring.\r\n[4]\r\nMore information about job openings will be posted on the Castellan Motors careers page in the coming months.</div>\r\n",
