      "slot": "question.79"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 181–185 refer to the following e-mail.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Mr. Quintero,\r\nThank you for the prompt shipment of our spring order, which arrived at our warehouse yesterday. Unfortunately, when our staff unpacked the boxes, they found that 18 of the 60 blue serving bowls were chipped or cracked. The damage seems to have been caused by a lack of packing material, as the bowls had been stacked directly on top of one another.\r\nWe would prefer replacements rather than a refund, since the bowls are featured in our summer catalog, which will be mailed to customers on 20 May. Could you let me know whether you can ship replacements before that date? I have attached photographs of the damaged items for your records. Our warehouse team has set the damaged bowls aside until we hear from you.\r\nIn addition, our stores in Brampton and Lisle have reported strong sales of your olive-green coffee mugs. I would like to add 120 of them to our next regular order in June.\r\nBest regards,\r\nOksana Petrenko\r\nSenior Buyer, Hollin &amp; Crane Home Goods</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Ms. Petrenko,\r\nI am very sorry about the condition of the bowls, and thank you for sending the photographs. We have already addressed the matter with our packing team, and your future orders will be packed with extra protective material.\r\nWe have 12 blue serving bowls in stock, and I will send them to you by express courier today at no charge. The remaining six will come from our next production run and should reach you by 16 May. Please do not return the damaged bowls; you may dispose of them or keep them for display purposes. Our shipping department will e-mail you the tracking number for today’s courier delivery this afternoon.\r\nI am delighted to hear that the olive-green mugs are selling well. Once again, please accept our apologies. As a thank-you for your patience, I will apply a 10 percent discount to the mugs in your June order.\r\nSincerely,\r\nRafael Quintero\r\nCustomer Accounts, Marlowe Ceramics</div>\r\n",
