      "slot": "question.84"
    },
    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 186–190 refer to the following advertisement.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Kettleby Coffee Roasters — Wholesale Program for Cafés and Restaurants</span>Kettleby has been roasting small-batch coffee in Wellmont since 2009. We buy our beans directly from growers in Colombia, Ethiopia, and Guatemala, and our buyers visit each partner farm at least once a year. Every bag is roasted to order, never taken from old stock. Our wholesale customers enjoy:\r\n• Freshly roasted beans, shipped within 48 hours of roasting\r\n• Free delivery on orders over $300 within the Wellmont area\r\n• A free barista training session for new wholesale customers (for up to four staff members)\r\n• Volume pricing: 5% off orders of 20–39 kg and 10% off orders of 40 kg or more\r\nAll beans are sold in 1 kg bags. Not sure which blend is right for your business? New customers can request a free sample pack of any three blends by calling 555-0148.\r\nAbout our training: Sessions last three hours and take place at our roastery on Denholm Street. Our head barista covers grinding, espresso extraction, and milk steaming. Additional staff members beyond the first four may join for $25 per person.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Kettleby Coffee Roasters — Wholesale Order Form</span>Special instructions: Please deliver before 7:00 A.M., as we open at 7:30. Our delivery entrance is at the side of the building on Pell Street. We would also like to arrange the training session for our staff.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Hello,\r\nOur first order arrived at 6:45 on Friday morning, well before we opened, which we really appreciated. The coffee has already been very popular with our customers, especially the espresso. Several customers have even asked whether they can buy bags of beans to brew at home. However, one item was short: we received only 10 of the House Blend bags we ordered. Could you please send the rest as soon as possible, ideally with an early-morning delivery like the first one? We are almost out.\r\nRegarding the training session, five of our baristas would like to attend. I understand that there is normally a limit, so I would be willing to pay for the additional person if necessary. Any weekday afternoon next week would suit us, as the café is quieter after 2:00 P.M. and I can manage without them for a few hours.\r\nFinally, we are thinking of adding a decaffeinated coffee to our menu. Is there any way we could try your decaf blend before ordering it?\r\nBest regards,\r\nYusuf Demir\r\nOwner, The Linden Tree Café</div>\r\n",
