    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 191–195 refer to the following job-posting.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Tour Coordinator — Solano Heritage Tours, Lisbon</span>Solano Heritage Tours, which offers walking and coach tours of Portugal’s historic towns, is seeking a full-time Tour Coordinator to plan itineraries, manage bookings, and support our team of guides. The coordinator will also respond to customer inquiries by phone and e-mail and help train new guides each spring.\r\nRequirements: at least two years of experience in the tourism industry; fluency in English and Portuguese; a valid driver’s license. Knowledge of a third language, especially Spanish or French, is strongly preferred. The successful candidate should be available to start on 1 September.\r\nTo apply, send a CV and cover letter to Marta Figueiredo at hr@solanotours.pt by 30 June. Interviews will be held during the week of 7 July at our office on Rua das Flores. Candidates living outside Lisbon may request a video interview.\r\nWe offer a competitive salary, 25 days of paid vacation, and free tours for employees’ family members.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Dear Ms. Figueiredo,\r\nPlease find attached my CV and cover letter for the Tour Coordinator position advertised on your Web site. For the past three years, I have worked as a guide for a cycling tour company in Porto, leading groups of up to fifteen visitors. Spanish is my first language, and I am also fluent in English and Portuguese. In my current role, I also manage the company’s online booking system and respond to customer reviews, which I believe has prepared me well for the planning side of the position.\r\nAlthough I live in Porto, I would prefer to travel to Lisbon for an interview so that I can meet your team in person. However, I will be leading a tour group in the Douro Valley from 7 to 9 July. I would therefore be grateful if my interview could be scheduled for later that week.\r\nI have also attached a reference letter from my current employer, Rota Verde Cycling Tours. Thank you for considering my application.\r\nSincerely,\r\nNicolás Iturbe</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Solano Heritage Tours — Tour Coordinator Interviews</span>Note: Tiago Mendes will be at the International Tourism Fair in Madrid on 11 July. Ana Ribeiro (Senior Guide) will take his place on the interview panel that day. Each interview will last about 45 minutes. Candidates attending in person should report to the reception desk on the second floor.</div>\r\n",
