    "\r\n\r\n<div class=\"ref\">Questions 196–200 refer to the following memo.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">As many of you know, Horizon Travel will launch a digital edition of the magazine in January. In addition to all the articles from the print edition, it will offer short videos, interactive maps, and a searchable archive of past issues. To prepare for the launch, I have scheduled a planning meeting for Thursday, 11 September, from 9:30 A.M. to noon in Conference Room B. Attendance is required for all section editors (News, Features, Culture, and City Guides) and members of the marketing team; other staff are welcome to attend.\r\nBefore the meeting, please read the draft project plan, which I have uploaded to the shared drive. If you would like to add an item to the agenda, send it to my assistant, Kofi Mensah, by Friday, 5 September. The final agenda will be distributed on Monday, 8 September. Staff who are unable to attend will receive a summary of the discussion the following week.\r\nLunch will be served in the staff lounge after the meeting for everyone who attends.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\"><span class=\"ttl\">Horizon Travel — Digital Edition Planning Meeting</span>Please bring a laptop or tablet to view the app prototype. Coffee and pastries will be available during the break.</div>\r\n<div class=\"passage\">Hi Beatriz,\r\nI’ve just learned that the photographer I hired for our Iceland feature can meet only on Thursday morning, because she flies to Reykjavik that afternoon. The Iceland story will be the cover feature of our February issue, so it’s important that everything goes smoothly. Since the shoot is scheduled for October, I really need to go over the details with her before she leaves. Would it be possible for me to swap slots with Carla? That way I could meet the photographer at 10:30 and still be back in plenty of time. I’ve already checked with Carla, and she doesn’t mind. Please let me know if the change works for you.\r\nAlso, I’ve read the project plan on the shared drive. The section on video assumes that each editor will film his or her own content, but most of us have no filming experience at all. I’d like to propose hiring a freelance video producer for the first six months, and I’ll include cost estimates in my presentation.\r\nThanks,\r\nEmeka</div>\r\n",
